mbarrier_wait(mbar_addr, expected_phase);

asm volatile("tcgen05.fence::after_thread_sync;");
```

## Load Results from Tensor Memory

The addressing uses `taddr + (row << 16) + col`:

> "Each `tcgen05.ld.sync.aligned.32x32b.x8.b32` call loads 8 FP32 values per thread (32 bytes)"

```cuda
for (int col = 0; col < BLOCK_N; col += 8) {
    int row = (warp_id * 32) << 16;
    int tmem_addr = tmem_base + row + col;

    asm volatile(
        "tcgen05.ld.sync.aligned.32x32b.x8.b32 {%0,%1,%2,%3,%4,%5,%6,%7}, [%8];"
        : "=f"(reg[0]), "=f"(reg[1]), /* ... */ "=f"(reg[7])
        : "r"(tmem_addr)
    );
}

asm volatile("tcgen05.wait::ld.sync.aligned;");
```

The key pattern is: **allocate → initialize mbarrier → loop with enable_input_d toggling → commit → wait → load from tmem → deallocate**.

